        "root_cause": "The actual CreateFileTransactedW data/main writers open existing names with Normal, without FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT. Version then checks the resolved target handle, not the substituted link entry. An admitted owned object moved outside its authorized root retains FileId/hash and can pass full Matches through a new symlink. Directory pins do not pin child file names. Microsoft documents that the omitted flag makes this API open and affect the symbolic-link target: [CreateFileTransactedW symbolic-link behavior](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winbase/nf-winbase-createfiletransactedw).",
        "severity": "must",
        "status": "open",
        "tests": [
          "Extend actual ModernMainPublication with a same-volume isolated sibling target: move admitted main, insert symlink in the pre-publication hook, verify the original target still has expected identity/bytes, then assert no leaked exception, no success, no external-target write/truncation, no partial journal/pending publication and no later MarkBlocked/retry adoption. The raw substitution finishes before the witness capture, so it is not the excluded active-during-capture writer case.",
          "Add a focused actual data/store counterpart for a redirected existing authorized object/parent as affected by the same opens, using only isolated roots. Preserve outside-target bytes and namespace entries. Do not touch real User.",
          "Single-point remove the actual writer no-follow/same-handle namespace rejection and require a successful build plus causal target-byte/identity/root-confinement Failed assertion, followed by restored-source Passed. Existing same-byte different-FileId CP29 is retained and does not discriminate the same-owned-FileId redirected case."
        ]
      },
